From f9f5930da20d10f5fb53a727d46cdc4ff83c3f04 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Drikus Roor <drikusroor@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 21:46:22 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] OpenTW: runtime terraforming (openmw.world.terrain)

Global Lua scripts can now change the land of the default worldspace while
the game runs:

  world.terrain.flatten(center, radius, height[, falloff])
  world.terrain.raise(center, radius, delta[, falloff])
  world.terrain.paint(center, radius, landTextureIdOrFile)
  world.terrain.reset()
  world.terrain.VERSION

- MWWorld::Terraformer keeps edited copies of LAND records. Brushes work on
  the global vertex grid so shared edge vertices stay equal (no seams), and
  recompute normals and min/max heights. Cells without land (open sea) can
  be edited too, starting from the flat sea floor.
- LandManager serves edited cells; RenderingManager/Terrain::World drop
  cached chunks and rebuild views (quadtree and grid); Scene swaps the
  physics and navmesh heightfields of loaded cells; actors in the area are
  put back on the ground.
- A painted texel may use a texture from another plugin than its land
  record (per-texel plugin in LandData); core.land.getTextureAt sees paint.
- Caches built from land data are only stored when the terraform revision
  did not change during the build (background preloading races).
- Edits are not saved: World::clear() resets them and mods replay their own
  edits after loading, so saves stay compatible with stock OpenMW.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
